! AlAs, nonmagnetic: a non-centrosymmetric **ultrasoft** crystal.
!
! The piezoelectric tensor is refused for an ultrasoft or PAW dataset, and the
! reason given was that "every ultrasoft and PAW case committed here is a
! centrosymmetric crystal whose tensor vanishes identically, so the strain leg
! has never been measured on one". That was not true the day it was written:
! `Al.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF` and `As.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF` were
! already committed, and `alas-magnetoelectric-nosoc.in` already built
! zincblende from them -- `ibrav = 2` with the basis at (0,0,0) and
! (1/4,1/4,1/4), which is precisely the non-polar, non-centrosymmetric class
! `require_a_nonpolar_crystal` names as the handled one.
!
! What that file is not is *nonmagnetic*: it sets `noncolin` and a `B_field`, so
! it is stopped upstream by the noncollinear branch of
! `require_a_sternheimer_regime` and never reaches the dataset refusal at all.
! This is the same cell with the magnetism taken out -- the missing twenty lines,
! so that the refusal can be argued about on the case rather than on a claim
! about the pseudopotential library.
!
! Symmetry is left **on**, unlike the magnetoelectric file: the strain response
! is symmetrised as a tensor and `genstrain` reduces the candidate strains with
! the crystal's group, so `nosym` there would be answering a different question.
!
! Same cutoffs as the magnetoelectric case, whose bands are validated against
! Elk along L-Gamma-X (0.062 eV rms on the valence manifold).
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 2, celldm(1) = 10.6134, nat = 2, ntyp = 2,
    ecutwfc = 25.0, ecutrho = 200.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
    mixing_beta = 0.7
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al 26.98 Al.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
 As 74.92 As.pbe-n-rrkjus_psl.1.0.0.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Al 0.00 0.00 0.00
 As 0.25 0.25 0.25
K_POINTS (automatic)
 4 4 4 0 0 0
